From: MinGit BusyBox Bundle maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] win32: query file ownership through the existing wide path

Based on git-for-windows/busybox-w32
 d8d8bb397f1e200ba5a871dc6aa4af819b23f32a.
Upstream BusyBox-w32 is maintained by Ron Yorston, originally ported by
Nguyễn Thái Ngọc Duy; Git for Windows carries additional downstream changes.
Source: https://github.com/git-for-windows/busybox-w32
Upstream: https://github.com/rmyorston/busybox-w32
Bundle integration changes: GPL-2.0-only; upstream attribution is unchanged.

The stat implementation already resolves file_name from UTF-8 into wpath
and uses wide APIs for attributes and compressed size. Its READ_CONTROL
handle still used CreateFileA, decoding the UTF-8 filename with the ANSI
code page. For Chinese filenames this failed, selected the existing
uid/gid zero fallback, and cleared other permissions. Nonadministrator ash
then rejected otherwise executable native children. CI 41929624612 showed
identical executable bytes and Windows owner/SDDL producing mode 755 for
an ASCII filename but 750 for its Chinese sibling.

Reuse wpath with CreateFileW. Retain READ_CONTROL, reparse-point handling,
owner checks, failure behavior and all mingw64_defconfig features. No new
conversion, allocation, manifest requirement or permission bypass is needed.
The existing real Unicode-path clone, hook and LFS gates remain unchanged.
---

diff --git a/win32/mingw.c b/win32/mingw.c
index aaf041e..abad6f2 100644
--- a/win32/mingw.c
+++ b/win32/mingw.c
@@ -1113,7 +1113,7 @@ static int do_lstat(int follow, const char *file_name, struct mingw_stat *buf)
 			flags = FILE_FLAG_BACKUP_SEMANTICS;
 			if (S_ISLNK(buf->st_mode))
 				flags |= FILE_FLAG_OPEN_REPARSE_POINT;
-			fh = CreateFile(file_name, READ_CONTROL, 0, NULL,
+			fh = CreateFileW(wpath, READ_CONTROL, 0, NULL,
 								OPEN_EXISTING, flags, NULL);
 			if (fh != INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE) {
 				if (GetFileInformationByHandle(fh, &hdata)) {
